WEBVTT

00:01:25.850 --> 00:01:30.000
When we land a tourer headquarters in Berlin, the Cold War reaches a new crisis.

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:34.440
Russians haul down the red flag, signifying Soviet withdrawal from the four-power command

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:37.200
that has governed Berlin since the war's end.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:41.240
Taking no pains to disguise the fact that they want the Western Allies out of Berlin,

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:48.060
the Reds begin a blockade of the city, tracks are removed from the roadbeds, and trains

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:51.080
are stopped for so-called technical reasons.

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:55.910
Barges carrying food and coal find the waterways suddenly closed to them, highways are blocked

00:01:55.910 --> 00:02:00.000
and deserted, the aim of the Russians to starve the entire city into submission back

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:05.890
fires completely. In the shadow of the Soviet sector, 300,000 Berliners gather in protest and

00:02:05.890 --> 00:02:11.730
pledge support to the Western Allies. Meanwhile, Anthony Eaton arrives in the German capital for

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:17.450
an emergency meeting, as does the French military commander, General Koenig. Later, America's General

00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:22.390
Lucius D. Clay, speaking for the Western Allies, announces their decision. We have a right to be

00:02:22.390 --> 00:02:28.260
in Berlin, and we intend to maintain that right. But how? Ask freedom-loving people the world over

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:30.000
and anxiously await the answer.

00:02:50.860 --> 00:02:55.640
of the 19th Troop Carrier Squadron report to 19th Operations immediately.

